A||||1||Rodney||L4 fan switch differences||||1||
Z||000000||Rodney||08-13-2001||08:40 PM||||It seems to be on the 84-86 L4 there are 2 styles of fan switches. The P-22 lists 2 different part numbers. One for non A/C and one for A/C cars. I have a A/C L4 owner that says it will not fit his wiring harness. Looking at the Helms manual they both seem to be the same as they both are a single wire and both turn on at 235 degrees. They both control a ground to a relay so the amperage load across them is similar. I willing to bet the thread pitch and diameter is the same. But the connector is different. I wonder why GM did this?? ||||reg||1
Z||000001||theogre||08-13-2001||09:30 PM||||Rodney,<P>Either switches are diferant, or he's trying to replace the wrong one.<P>There's a bunch of L4 AC cars that have 2 speed fans and have 2 switches with a total of three contacts. (One switch is the 235 job and the other has 2 sets of contacts...)<P>That setup already has one set of contacts that run at lower temperature. (221F on, 212F off) This switch also has another set of contacts that only run the high speed fan line.<P>The other switch should be the same as all the others use. This one also is tied to the low speed. It turns on at 235F and has a single contact.<P>You can view the wiring diagram for more details. If you don't have a manual they are online here... <A HREF="http://www.euronet.nl/users/fo_elmo/fiero.htm" TARGET=_blank>http://www.euronet.nl/users/fo_elmo/fiero.htm</A>  you'll need acrobat reader to see them||||reg||1
